  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building for Prevention of Corruption</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant seeks to provide technical assistance to ICPC, a critical agency in Nigeria&apos;s effort to restore rule of law and fiduciary accountability, so that it develops a clear strategic focus and gains adequate operational capacity and confidence to lead the fight against corruption in Nigeria. The World Bank intends to contribute towards this joint effort  through the proposed IDF grant.  The mainA central purpose of the grant will be to assist the ICPC to develop a robust anti-corruption strategy in cooperation with civil society stakeholders and other public watchdog agencies, and to convey lessons learned from the experience of countries which have established similar anti-corruption agencies and the difficulties they have encountered running effective institutions. The following activities will be supported by the grant and they are critical in giving ICPC the strategic focus, the right skills, knowledge and confidence to lead the fight against corruption in Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
